think Picked up the thread from crux/REMEMBER + the top three session-log recommends. Live edge is the Season G open-media image family; last lap landed image/euler_number.rye (single-region topology by bit-quad counting). Standfast checked: every living REDS row (80, 83, 84, 85, 81/82/86/87 prose) is closed or released, only #75 rests as custody-gated errata (a deep-debride gate, not agent-closable). No open agent-closable red -- proceed to the next lap.
think The card named two crux-first next siblings: the inscribed-versus-enclosing roundness reconciliation, or a multi-component Euler read. Weighed them Lindy-first crux-first. The roundness read is thrice-flagged as genuine multi-lap work (chamfer-inradius 3-4 units against hull-Euclidean circumradius; a naive inradius<=circumradius really flips on a compact 5x5 square -- inradius 3.0 vs circumradius 2.828; reconciling wants a shared continuous convention, the Chebyshev center generally irrational). Crux-first wants the hardest SOLVABLE move, not the impossible dream that never closes; the roundness read does not close in one clean lap. The multi-component read drops a limiting assumption (more capable, more durable -- Lindy) and closes cleanly by composing over label + euler_number. Approved my own design round: the multi-component read.
think The key exactness insight, checked before coding: label.rye gives 8-connected components, so two foreground pixels in one 2x2 bit-quad window are 8-adjacent, hence one component -- so no window ever straddles two objects, and the whole-foreground tally is byte-for-byte the SUM of the per-object tallies. Topological additivity is therefore EXACT here, provable on metal, and it is the decisive crux: read the scene two ways (one whole-foreground sweep vs the sum of per-object euler_number calls) and assert they agree.
think Built image/euler_scene.rye: scene_euler (one any-foreground bit-quad sweep), scene_topology (per-component holes via euler_number per label, plus the additivity assertions), and reads total_holes / holed_component_count / most_holed / is_all_simply_connected over a SceneTopology carrying a per-component hole slice. Compose not braid -- owns only the whole sweep, the aggregation, and the reads; label owns the component map, euler_number owns the single-region theorem it sums.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run after one build-type fix only (a u64 holes_sum needed @intCast to i64 in an assert; @as could not narrow) -- no algorithm red. The three-object scene (block E1, ring E0, twice-pierced E-1) read total Euler 0 = 1+0+(-1), three components, three holes, the single sweep agreeing with the per-object sum; per-object holes [0,1,2]; holed_component_count 2; most_holed the pierced block; a filled two-block scene total Euler 2, all simply connected; an empty scene a valid zero topology, most_holed refusing NoComponents; determinism.
obs TAME caught a compound assert (best_label >= 1 and best_label <= components) and I split it into two named halves, re-GREEN. width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, living-card ASCII GREEN. Chose most_holed to break ties by the earliest label (strictly-greater comparison) for determinism.
obs Council rota lap (item 21, cycling from euler_number's item 20) deep-read ORGANIZING.md -- reinforcing that module code lives in its module home (image/), witnesses in tools/, the README compresses the record, and the session log records what happened while TASKS holds what is next; this lap's placement follows that shape exactly.
